A||N||26||Boomtastic||"Holy Red Intake Duct Batman!"||||3||
Z||000000||Boomtastic||09-09-2001||10:36 AM||||A while back, I picked up a new intake duct (that black rubber piece), but in thermorubberized red, and a free flow air filter. Well, I finally got it installed on my Formula, and let me say that it wasn't easy because frankly, I don't believe this even fits a Fiero (or ever did!). The bends were not as close as the originals were, which meant that I had to install it pointing in a downward fashion. Plus, there was no provision for the tube that comes off of the rear valve cover. Add to that that you have to do "something" with the MAT sensor (the air temp sensor that is screwed into the side of the air cleaner) and you can see that their were a few obstacles to overcome. Here's how the install looks:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_1_1.jpg"> <P>How I solved everything was this way - the intake duct was rotated 90° and mounted so that the air cleaner end pointed down. This placed the air cleaner above the original opening of the old air box. (All of the air cleaner housing and brackets were removed, but the water separator was left. It's serving no real purpose, so I didn't remove it.) The MAT sensor was plugged in and slipped into the opening of the water separator, from above. This will give the ECM some reading of the temperature of the air "around" the nose of the free flow air filter. The tube that came off of the rear valve cover too the most work. I cut it approx. 1" to the left of the bracket that bolts it to the head. I then crimped the pipe to that I could screw an air fitting (like you would use on an air tool) into it. Lots of pipe joint compound to seal it was installed during the assembly. The air fitting threaded right into the pipe. On the opposite end, I installed a "ricer" style breather. Sadly, the "ricer" breather was the only style I could get that had a small opening. Thank goodness for those little Jap cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> The breather is held on by a small heather hose clamp. Here's a closeup:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/intake_1.jpg"> <P>It sounds great, and the engine, which was starving for air before, has responded quite well to the extra flow. (Engine is not stock - it's been bored .060 over and stuffed with go fast goodies) <P>What do you think?<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||RedOktober||09-09-2001||04:24 PM||||Love It. Where did u pick it up from???<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red6[1]a.jpg">  <BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000002||gt boy||09-09-2001||04:37 PM||||hey..that looks great ...but i have another question. <P>what are you using to take your pics with??  the quality is outstanding!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>p.s....what type of "go fast goodies" are we talking about here?<P><BR>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."<p>[This message has been edited by gt boy (edited 09-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Boomtastic||09-09-2001||05:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RedOktober:<BR><B>Love It. Where did u pick it up from???<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>RedOktober - eBay! It came from a guy in CA. I'll see if I can't find his email addy. He only does a few of these at a time. I offered for him to do mine and he declined! Strange ..<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Boomtastic||09-09-2001||05:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gt boy:<BR><B>what are you using to take your pics with??  the quality is outstanding!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks! I'm using a Sony DSC-F505V digital camera and editing the photos (if necessary) with Adobe Photoshop 6.01.<P><B>p.s....what type of "go fast goodies" are we talking about here?</B><P>The engine was built by Jeg's Racing in Ohio with no expense spared. It's a 2.8 bored .060 over with mild porting on the heads & intake manifolds. The engine was line-bored and balanced during the rebuild. Fuel is supplied by Accel injectors and controlled by a JET chip. Exhaust manifolds have been replaced with Fiero Store Sprint headers (still have to work on the rest of the exhaust). An MSD 6AL controls the ignition, flowing through Accel 8.8 Pro Race wires. Immediate plans call for a 100hp NOS shot, and future plans have a turbo unit slated for install ... once I get done with the sound system (needs to be upgraded, again).<BR><P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
